chat_models.py,chatbot/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py,7370bad9be7593d3bf4fa55558e33ed94a8539af,gamzeozgul/chatbot,https://api.github.com/repositories/846704329/contents/chatbot/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py?ref=874230bf005db07514e63fb738eeec1680817dc2,https://api.github.com/repositories/846704329/git/blobs/7370bad9be7593d3bf4fa55558e33ed94a8539af,https://github.com/gamzeozgul/chatbot/blob/874230bf005db07514e63fb738eeec1680817dc2/chatbot/Lib/site-packages/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py,,,0,0,0,4,2025-04-08T14:09:46Z,0,0,"# 🤖 Chatbot

A simple chatbot built in Python that simulates a command-line conversation with the user.  
Great for learning basic interaction logic, command parsing, and improving Python CLI scripting skills.

## 🧠 Features

- Supports simple commands and keyword-based responses  
- Handles user input and returns conversational replies  
- Easily extendable with new commands and behaviors  

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Python 3.6 or higher

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/gamzeozgul/chatbot.git
cd chatbot
```

### Run

```bash
python chatbot.py
```

## 💡 Example Interaction

```txt
You: hello  
Bot: Hi there! How can I help you?

You: tell me a joke  
Bot: Why don’t scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything!

You: bye  
Bot: Goodbye! Have a great day.
```

## 🛠️ Built With

- Python 🐍

## 📌 To-Do

- Add support for more natural language variations  
- Store conversation history  
- Improve response matching logic  

